# ==============================================================================
# CodeFolio Client Environment Configuration (.env.example)
# ==============================================================================
# This file defines the frontend environment variables for CodeFolio.
# Vite requires custom environment variables to be prefixed with "VITE_".
#
# Usage:
#   1. Copy this file to '.env.local' (for local overrides) or configure inside
#      your hosting platform's build settings (e.g. Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare).
#   2. Do NOT commit real production secrets into version control.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend API Base URL
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Defines where the Axios API client directs requests.
#
# Option A: Vercel Reverse Proxy (Recommended & Default):
#   When deploying to Vercel using the root vercel.json rewrite configuration,
#   Vercel automatically proxies '/api/*' to your Render backend.
#   In this setup, VITE_API_URL should remain '/api' (or be left unset).
#   No environment variable is needed in the Vercel dashboard!
#   This guarantees that session and CSRF cookies (HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict)
#   are treated by browsers as first-party same-origin cookies.
#
# Option B: Direct Cross-Origin Backend:
#   If you bypass the Vercel proxy rewrite and connect directly to Render,
#   set VITE_API_URL to your Render service URL:
#     VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend-name.onrender.com/api
#   Note: Requires matching CORS configuration in Render (CLIENT_URL).
#
VITE_API_URL=/api
